        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm trying to pin down the root — it looks like क्षिव् (kṣiv), meaning \"to spit/eject,\" found in the bhvādi class as parasmaipada, though the Dhatupatha groups it with ष्ठिव् under the sense \"निरसन\" (ejecting), and I want to confirm its classification before forming the perfect.\n\nFor the 3rd person dual perfect, I get चिक्षिवतुः: since the ending is kit (atuḥ), guṇa of the short इ doesn't apply, and the hali ca lengthening rule doesn't trigger here because the व् is followed by a vowel rather than a consonant. The reduplicated क्ष् becomes च् via kuhoścuḥ, giving चिक्षिवतुः.\n\n",
